---
title: Picidae
---
# Picidae

Picidae is the woodpecker family, specialists in extracting insects from wood
and in excavating cavities in it. The skull carries a spongy, shock-absorbing
plate and the hyoid apparatus loops around the back of the head to anchor a
barbed tongue that can be extended far beyond the bill. Stiffened tail feathers
brace the body against a trunk while the bill works. Drumming rather than song
carries territorial information in most species. See
[[great-spotted-woodpecker]].
